## Q: Which industries have the highest average shortfall probability?
status=COMPLETED  (13.6s)
Genie: You want to see which industries have the highest average probability of running out of cash soon, expressed as a percentage. The results also show how many accounts are in each industry. The list is sorted to show the industries with the highest average shortfall probability first, and industries with the same average are sorted alphabetically.
SQL:
SELECT
  `industry`,
  ROUND(AVG(`shortfall_prob`) * 100, 1) AS `avg_shortfall_pct`,
  COUNT(*) AS `account_count`
FROM `serverless_stable_0dcqtv_catalog`.`smb_cashflow`.`account_cashflow_health`
WHERE `industry` IS NOT NULL
  AND `shortfall_prob` IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY `industry`
ORDER BY AVG(`shortfall_prob`) DESC, `industry` ASC
Result: industry | avg_shortfall_pct | account_count
